otal":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested in: v4.4.beta3.official [06acfccf8]\nNot effected: pre-4.4, project.godot does not support UID\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.beta3 - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4080 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6636) - AMD Ryzen 9 7950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you set a Main Scene it will always open/load this Scene in the Editor when you launch. This does not respect `open_scenes` that are saved in `.godot/editor/editor_layout.cfg`. If the Scene is closed, it should not force-open anytime the Editor is launched.\n\nManually editing `project.godot` to use the `res://` path to the Main Scene, will not force-open unless `open_scenes` list is empty.\n(force-opening the Main Scene when the list is empty is the same behavior as 4.3)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSet a Main Scene (by any of the 3 methods), and close this newly set Main Scene.\nClose the Editor, and open the project from the Project List window.\n(Reload Current Project does not reproduce this issue)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nA blank project with two saved Scenes, first set as the Main Scene and closed, second Scene opened.","closed_by":{"login":"Red3Tango","id":13739585,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNzM5NTg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13739585?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red3Tango","html_url":"https://github.com/Red3Tango","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red3Tango/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red3Tango/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red3Tango/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red3Tango/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Red